{"context":"Execution state today lives in .eka/execution-state.md (scope, mode, items, current/next, decisions) — git-ignored, not a CKO, not in canonical store, not synced across devices. Users work on multiple devices and lose state. Status needs a proper CKO source so eka status can show current state deterministically. Must respect EKA invariants: immutability (new revision per update, never mutation), strata (Execution stratum), traceability, and transport semantics (snapshot vs workspace-native). Related: adr:009/011/012 (runtime/immutability/CKO), adr:010/032 (sync/adoption), eka status contract (adr:036).","decision":"Define execution-state snapshot as a ses- CKO (Execution, stratum 4) with content keys: scope (ctr reference), items (work item refs + executionState), current, next, decisions, mode. Lifecycle: planned/active/completed via standard stratum transitions; each update = new instanceVersion with changeLog. Storage: repo-attributed via snapshot (so eka sync push transports it) — workspace-native only if explicitly adopted. eka status in repo-scoped mode reads latest ses for that repo's active container/scope and renders single 'current' projection; full history via eka get ses:\u003cid\u003e --timeline. Migration: one-time conversion of .eka/execution-state.md into ses-1, then retire markdown.","consequences":"Positive: execution state becomes immutable, content-addressed, queryable via eka get ses:\u003cid\u003e and eka status, syncable across devices via snapshot (repo-attributed) or workspace-native + adopt flow — solves cross-device sync. Negative: existing .eka/execution-state.md must be migrated/retired; tooling must adopt new ses lifecycle. Neutral: status only renders latest instanceVersion as 'current state' — history preserved via instanceVersion lineage, not shown by default.","alternativesConsidered":"A) New token family (e.g., stt/exs) for execution state — rejected: closed token set, adds standard change. B) Reuse ctr- workItems prose key — rejected: never parsed for membership, breaks invariants. C) Reuse ses- (session) as execution-state snapshot — viable: ses belongs to Execution domain, already tracks orchestration. D) Reuse run- (Operations) — rejected: wrong stratum (Operations is lowest, execution-state is Execution). E) Keep markdown .eka/execution-state.md + git-track it — rejected: still file-prose, no CKO guarantees, violates immutable model. Chosen: C) ses-based CKO + optional lightweight spec defining content shape.","status":"proposed"}